# Git is only half of what keeps the published folder clean, and the smaller half.
#
# Steam does not read .gitignore at all. SteamUGC.SetItemContent takes the junction's target
# directory as it stands on disk, with no filtering, so anything sitting in the published folder
# is published. That is what `Mod/` is for: the junction points there, and everything else in
# this repository - Art/, the docs, this file - stays out of reach by construction.

# Claude Code session worktrees and local settings: each worktree is a full copy of this
# repository, and they are never shared.
.claude/

# Development environments.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo

# System.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Generated textures. The game, or a tool, writes a .dds cache beside each PNG in Mod/Textures. They
# are never tracked and never wanted: the PNG is the source. Steam sends the folder as it stands on
# disk, so six of them travelled with the 0.1.0 upload (see CHANGELOG.md); the publication CI sends
# tracked files only.
*.dds

# Windows Explorer folder icons (Art/ModIcon.ico, Art/Preview.ico), local to this machine and never
# part of the mod. desktop.ini is ignored above.
*.ico

# Test and preview evidence lives on disk and never in git: captures and logs grow without limit.
# What is worth keeping is one line per run in docs/runs/, and the few files named in STATUS.md.
Tests/Pickle/Evidence/
evidence/
Art/preview-qa/
